Done. Both changes build cleanly, existing tests pass, and the CLI behaves correctly end-to-end.

**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note>`: iterates notes in order, keeping those whose `tags` contain an exact `tag` match (`contains` on the `Vec<String>`), preserving relative order.

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — the `list` command now scans `--tag <TAG>` from the args; when present it runs `notekeep::filter_by_tag`, otherwise it lists all notes as before.

Verified behavior (fresh data dir):
- `list` → all 3 notes
- `list --tag rust` → the two `#rust` notes, in original order
- `list --tag python` → the one `#python` note
- `list --tag nonexistent` → nothing

One note on the `--tag` parsing: it takes the value immediately following the flag and ignores any trailing positional args. That matches the existing simple CLI style; if you'd prefer stricter handling (e.g. erroring on unknown flags or `--tag=rust` syntax), say so and I'll tighten it.


